<card id="c" title="Zla Kolata and Prokletije: 300 Euros There and Back">
<do type="prev" label="Back"><prev/></do>
<p>I opened Google Maps. Yep, it was Podgorica. The bus was almost 3 hours ahead of schedule.</p>
<p>And there I am, standing at the Podgorica bus station with a twenty-kilo backpack. Everything&apos;s closed, I haven&apos;t booked a hotel, the bus to Gusinje isn&apos;t until 8:45, and every bench inside the station is taken by sleeping tourists.</p>
<p>At first I just put the backpack in a corner. But there&apos;s no luggage storage at the station, so when I went wandering, I had to haul all twenty kilos with me. For a while I walked around the station and the area. Strolled over to the train station, it&apos;s right next door. Waited for the nearest bakery to open at 5:30 and went for breakfast.</p>
<p>Kiflice, still warm, with cheese and with jam, and a yogurt. I was so hungry I didn&apos;t even get around to taking a photo.</p>
